    "body": "fix on issue/790-vendor-step-guide · PR mkinney/Camcraft#1 (draft) · docs only, no test pinned · merges when reviewed\n\nImport check (local vendor inputs, names generic, nothing committed):\n\n| Input | Imports | Time | Triangles | Units | Bounds vs published drawing | Mark as fixture | detect_holes |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| vendor fixture plate STEP (inch) | yes | 0.43 s | 34,044 | declared inch, scaled to mm | X and Y match; Z differs from the drawing by 0.10 in (unresolved) | works | 471 found, matches the published hole count |\n| vendor subplate STEP | yes | 0.65 s | 3,748 | declared inch | not compared (no overall size on the sheet read) | works | 5 found (not compared) |\n| vendor modular vise STEP, single station | yes | 0.22 s | 4,585 | declared inch | no axis matches the drawing's overall length (likely a different configuration; needs a human look) | works | 19 found (not compared) |\n| vendor modular vise STEP, dual station | yes | 0.21 s | 3,480 | declared inch | not compared | works | not run |\n\nBodies: one model per import; the MCP does not expose a body count. No importer bug proven, so no bug issue filed.\nGuide: docs/user-guide/vendor-fixtures.md (no user-guide folder on main; docs site #777 still open).\n",
